  "script": "The Maybach S680 demands attention with its bold chrome multi-slat grille, epitomizing luxury and presence. Its distinctive two-tone paint \u2013 a silver top over deep blue \u2013 marks the S680\u2019s luxurious design. Inside, the striking contrast between deep blue leather and sleek wood with ambient lighting defines opulence. Under the hood lies a powerful 6.0-liter V12, boasting 621 horsepower and 738 lb-ft of torque. Rear diamond-stitched leather seats come with plush headrests, ensuring unmatched comfort for passengers. The front seats' quilted leather with contrasting blue stitching exemplifies Mercedes Maybach's craftsmanship. The sleek black lower body and elegant silver upper section highlights the Maybach's luxurious styling. Diamond-stitched blue leather on the door panel enhances the luxury feel, with detailed attention from Maybach. Maybach-branded pedals in the footwell emphasize the vehicle's status and premium attention to detail. This powerhouse matches directly against the Bentley Flying Spur. While the Maybach packs 621 hp, the Bentley offers 626 hp. The Maybach S680 started around $200K new. Today, it trades for about $160K, reflecting an 8% annual depreciation. Would you choose the luxurious and powerful S680 over its competitors? Let us know your thoughts below!",
